  "hostKind": "node",
  "description": "Procedural floor plan where EVERYTHING is a COMPOSED CHILD COMPONENT — walls, doors, windows and furniture are `ref` instances of the library Wall / Door / Window / Bed / Wardrobe / Sofa / TV / Table / Toilet / Sink objects — so each instance is individually selectable (Components list / canvas click), per-instance overridable, and REPOSITIONABLE from Properties without touching the canvas. Walls: each wall run is a Wall child (`wall[k]` / wall_s…) with its LENGTH driven by the plan and its THICKNESS + HEIGHT soft-bound — editable per wall; perimeter runs extend half a thickness past the corners so joints close flush in 2D and 3D. Doors/windows: `_pos` slider slides each along ITS wall (clamped clear of corners); every instance also takes Offset X/Y + Rotate nudges. `rectangular` = seeded BSP into `rooms` cells (Random Layout jitters; Seed repeats); a Door per partition + entrance (door[0..n]), a Window per facade (window[0..3], bottom one defaults beside the entrance), and — with Furnish on — rooms get ROLES by size: the largest is the LIVING room (Sofa + TV unit + dining Table), the smallest (≥3 rooms) is the BATHROOM (Toilet + Sink), the rest are BEDROOMS (Bed + Wardrobe); each piece is placed along its room's boundary, back to the wall facing inward, with its own `_pos` slider (0–100 around the room perimeter). `L-shape` / `T-shape` / `I-shape` / `C-shape` / `Z-shape` / `stepped` = rectilinear shells decomposed into non-overlapping rectangular CELLS (L/T = 2–3 arms; I = top+bottom flanges + central web; C/U = back bar + two arms around an open courtyard; Z/S = two offset bars + a linking stem; stepped = `Staircase Steps` left-aligned bands terracing inward). Each cell is seeded-BSP'd into rooms INDEPENDENTLY (a room never spans the shape's inner corner), the arm/band seams become partition walls with a connecting Door, and the entrance Door + Windows + furniture compose onto every shape exactly as in `rectangular`. `Spine / Corridor` (have_spine) threads a circulation corridor of `Spine Width` down the LONGEST axis of each cell (centred → central for a rectangle, an L of two runs for `L-shape`, one per arm/band otherwise); the BSP then fills only the FLANKING space either side (never the spine), and every room off the corridor gets its own Door onto it. North arrow optional. Footprint W×D derives from Rooms × Avg Area at the given Aspect; origin = node centre.",
